# Local secrets for `npm run dev`. Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored).
# Production secrets go through `wrangler secret put <NAME>`, never the repo.
# Add names here as tickets introduce them.

# Keep a .dev.vars file even if it's empty: without one, wrangler falls back to .env
# and would expose every .env/.env.local variable to the Worker (and to `wrangler types`).

# STM-5: Clerk JWKS public key (Clerk dashboard → API keys → JWKS Public Key, PEM).
# The Worker verifies session tokens with it, networkless. Keep the line breaks inside
# double quotes. Production: pbpaste | npx wrangler secret put CLERK_JWT_KEY
# CLERK_JWT_KEY="<paste the whole PEM here, BEGIN/END lines and line breaks included>"

# STM-13: R2 API token for presigning upload URLs (Cloudflare dashboard → R2 →
# Manage API tokens → Object Read & Write, scoped to createmyq-uploads and
# createmyq-uploads-dev). Production: npx wrangler secret put R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID / R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
# Local dev signs for (and, via the remote binding, reads) the dev bucket, never production.
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# UPLOADS_BUCKET_NAME=createmyq-uploads-dev

# STM-18: question generation through AI Gateway (the URL is a var in wrangler.jsonc).
# Production: npx wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# The kill switch is off in wrangler.jsonc; turn it on locally to generate.
# GENERATION_ENABLED=true
